using Global

~ interview_start

Noman: Sit down, Jason.

Noman: No need to make this complicated. You know why you're here.

Noman: You're leaving. Gunman Corp would like to make sure that stays a quiet, uneventful thing for everyone.

- What's the offer? [if compliance >= 0]
	Jason: Let's skip ahead. What's the offer?
	do compliance += 1
	=> deal_offer

- I haven't decided I need anything from you. [if leverage >= 0]
	Jason: I haven't decided I need anything from you, Noman.
	do leverage += 2
	do compliance -= 1
	=> deal_pushback

- I don't know what you're talking about.
	Jason: I don't know what you're talking about.
	do compliance -= 1
	do leverage += 1
	=> deal_deny

~ deal_offer

Noman: Straightforward. I like that.

Noman: A severance package. Generous. Signed NDA, and this conversation never happened.

do compliance += 1

=> deal_pivot

~ deal_pushback

Noman: (a thin smile) Careful. That sounded like a negotiation.

Noman: I can do negotiation. Just know there's a version of this where I don't need to.

do leverage += 1

=> deal_pivot

~ deal_deny

Noman: Jason. You closed the deal with three buyers who shouldn't exist on paper. I have the emails.

Noman: We're well past pretending.

do compliance -= 1

=> deal_pivot

~ deal_pivot

Noman: Let's not waste each other's time. Walk me through the first one. The one that started all this.

Jason: (The first buyer. The number that changed everything.)

do Global.trigger_flashback(1, "res://dialogues/interview_room_01.dialogue", "post_flashback_01")

=> END

~ post_flashback_01

Noman: (reads a note) "Compliance handles compliance." Cute line. Whose was it?

- It was mine. I own it. [if compliance >= 0]
	Jason: Mine. I said it. I meant it, too, back then.
	do compliance += 1
	=> shipment_lead_owned

- My manager's. He fed me that line. [if leverage >= 0]
	Jason: My manager's. He's the one who sold me on it.
	do leverage += 1
	=> shipment_lead_deflect

- I don't remember saying that.
	Jason: I don't remember saying that.
	do compliance -= 1
	=> shipment_lead_deny

~ shipment_lead_owned

Noman: Good. Ownership's useful — for both of us.

Noman: Tell me about the first shipment. Not the sale. The part where you signed off on it.

=> shipment_pivot

~ shipment_lead_deflect

Noman: Convenient. Everyone's manager fed them a line eventually.

Noman: Tell me about the first shipment anyway. The one you signed off on.

do compliance -= 1

=> shipment_pivot

~ shipment_lead_deny

Noman: You don't remember. Sure.

Noman: The shipment logs remember for you. Walk me through it.

do leverage -= 1

=> shipment_pivot

~ shipment_pivot

Jason: (The shipment. Marcus asking questions he already knew the answers to.)

do Global.trigger_flashback(2, "res://dialogues/interview_room_01.dialogue", "post_flashback_02")

=> END

~ post_flashback_02

Noman: Marcus. He still works here, you know.

Noman: Doesn't talk much anymore, from what I hear.

- That's not on me. [if compliance >= 0]
	Jason: That's not on me. He made his choice same as I made mine.
	do compliance += 1
	=> close_call_deflect

- I know. I think about that. [if leverage >= 0]
	Jason: I know. I think about that more than you'd guess.
	do leverage += 1
	=> close_call_owned

- I'd rather talk about something else.
	Jason: I'd rather talk about something else.
	do compliance -= 1
	=> close_call_avoid

~ close_call_deflect

Noman: Sure. Everyone made their choice.

Noman: Someone almost unmade yours, though. Internal audit, few months back. Tell me about that.

=> close_call_pivot

~ close_call_owned

Noman: (a flicker of something — surprise, maybe) Noted.

Noman: There was an internal audit that got close to your accounts. Walk me through it.

do leverage += 1

=> close_call_pivot

~ close_call_avoid

Noman: We don't get to choose the topics, Jason. That's not how this works.

Noman: The internal audit. The one that almost found you. Talk.

do compliance -= 1

=> close_call_pivot

~ close_call_pivot

Jason: (Someone in finance had noticed. For three days, Jason didn't sleep.)

do Global.trigger_flashback(3, "res://dialogues/interview_room_01.dialogue", "post_flashback_03")

=> END

~ post_flashback_03

Noman: Priya. Finance. She never filed a formal complaint, you know. That's unusual.

- I made sure of that. [if leverage >= 0]
	Jason: I made sure of that, one way or another.
	do leverage += 1
	=> buyer_returns_lead_owned

- People let things go. [if compliance >= 0]
	Jason: People let things go, Noman. It doesn't have to mean anything.
	do compliance += 1
	=> buyer_returns_lead_soft

- I'd rather not think about that one.
	Jason: I'd rather not think about that one.
	do compliance -= 1
	=> buyer_returns_lead_avoid

~ buyer_returns_lead_owned

Noman: Efficient. That's one word for it.

Noman: Let's talk about six months ago. The buyer who came back wanting more.

=> buyer_returns_pivot

~ buyer_returns_lead_soft

Noman: Some things mean something whether you want them to or not.

Noman: Six months ago. The buyer who came back wanting more. Tell me.

do compliance -= 1

=> buyer_returns_pivot

~ buyer_returns_lead_avoid

Noman: You don't get to skip the parts that are uncomfortable, Jason. That's the whole exercise.

Noman: Six months ago. The buyer who came back. Talk.

do leverage -= 1

=> buyer_returns_pivot

~ buyer_returns_pivot

Jason: (Volkov. Back again. Wanting more than software this time.)

do Global.trigger_flashback(4, "res://dialogues/interview_room_01.dialogue", "post_flashback_04")

=> END

~ post_flashback_04

if Global.priya_path == "escalated" and Global.escalation_backfired:
	Noman: One more thing, while we're on finance. That director you looped in on the Priya account.
	Noman: He mentioned it to someone he shouldn't have. Nothing came of it. This time.
	do Global.leverage -= 1
elif Global.priya_path == "escalated":
	Noman: That director you looped in on the Priya account, incidentally — kept his mouth shut. You got lucky there.

Noman: That's the meeting that shows up in your resignation timeline, actually. Two days later, you filed.

Noman: So let's finish where this all ends. Your last day. Your terminal. What did you do with it.

- Tell him straight. [if compliance >= 0]
	Jason: I'll tell you exactly what I did.
	do compliance += 1
	=> reckoning_lead_straight

- Make him work for it. [if leverage >= 0]
	Jason: That depends on what it's worth to you to know.
	do leverage += 1
	=> reckoning_lead_pressed

- Stay quiet.
	Jason: (says nothing)
	do compliance -= 1
	do leverage -= 1
	=> reckoning_lead_silent

~ reckoning_lead_straight

Noman: Appreciated. Go on, then.

=> reckoning_pivot

~ reckoning_lead_pressed

Noman: (a short, humorless laugh) There it is. Fine. Let's find out what it's worth.

do leverage += 1

=> reckoning_pivot

~ reckoning_lead_silent

Noman: Silence, this late in the conversation, is its own confession.

Noman: Your last day. Go on.

do compliance -= 1

=> reckoning_pivot

